# The build context is the source and nothing else.
#
# .git alone is 1.2 GiB here, and every byte of it is uploaded to the builder
# before the first instruction runs.
.git

# Build output and installed dependencies are REPRODUCED by the build. Sending a
# working tree's copies makes the image depend on the machine that built it —
# and `npm ci` and `go build` would then be layering onto someone else's results.
**/node_modules
webapp/channels/dist

